Keep Cloudflare named IP lists in sync with the router's WAN egress IP(s).
One named IP list per configured WAN interface.

The router is the DHCP client for the WAN, so it knows the egress IP
natively -- no external echo services, no polling, no third-party claims.
On every interval the plugin reads each configured WAN interface's current
IPv4 (and optionally global IPv6) address, compares with the last known
state, and only calls the Cloudflare Lists API when something changed.

Credential design: the plugin needs exactly ONE Cloudflare API permission
(Account -> Account Rulesets -> Edit). It cannot touch DNS, tunnels, tokens,
Access policies, or billing. The token is entered manually in the plugin UI
and stored in the OPNsense configuration.

